                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "471ad695-91a0-31a0-bdd7-7b36b87f70f1",
                        "entry_id": "bcf52278-0c3a-325f-9a25-c260155c982c",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Unshakable;",
                            "Firm; solid."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "25af41e7-c7e5-4eaf-96e7-e083b9d2d045",
                                "sense_id": "471ad695-91a0-31a0-bdd7-7b36b87f70f1",
                                "text": "an inconcussible foundation"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "08c5a466-f4c5-4ab8-bac0-f1eb2bd24418",
                                "sense_id": "471ad695-91a0-31a0-bdd7-7b36b87f70f1",
                                "text": "Who were they that did put far away the evil day, and, in despite of the prophet's threatenings, did flatter themselves in the conceit of their firm and inconcussible estate; but they who were at ease in Zion, who trusted upon mountains of Samaria, who lay upon beds of ivory, and stretched themselves upon their couches?"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "86e92dfb-2045-4e8c-a413-13d28dd2beaf",
                                "sense_id": "471ad695-91a0-31a0-bdd7-7b36b87f70f1",
                                "text": "Well, then, the Protestant establishments and the Protestant Bible are to fall together, and the Holy See alone to remain inconcussible."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "a8d84df7-4375-4e58-88d4-f239695c8520",
                                "sense_id": "471ad695-91a0-31a0-bdd7-7b36b87f70f1",
                                "text": "One writer puts forth \"Meditations on a Table,\" and from observing a crack in that article of furniture, draws the obvious moral that \"true fame must be built on the inconcussible rock of virtue.\""
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "1713b21b-926b-46fb-b93c-89247be4e509",
                                "sense_id": "471ad695-91a0-31a0-bdd7-7b36b87f70f1",
                                "text": "Truth is inconcussible — forever exempt from all transient vicissitudes, albeit never dead and formal, always vibrant and adaptable — radiantly alive."
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "093d1698-033c-3e27-9752-623bb4855f67",
                        "entry_id": "bcf52278-0c3a-325f-9a25-c260155c982c",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Unshakable;",
                            "Unwavering; steadfast."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "602cc0cb-554a-45f9-aa51-dc7aa21f472b",
                                "sense_id": "093d1698-033c-3e27-9752-623bb4855f67",
                                "text": "an inconcussible conviction"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "eec3fc50-00b9-4d77-8199-40e3d5d7ff0a",
                                "sense_id": "093d1698-033c-3e27-9752-623bb4855f67",
                                "text": "What he called the \"pure ether\" and \"transparent\" texture of the triumphant Notion were assertions of the necessary reality, the inconcussible certainty of fact that had become pellucid."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "eb244ab3-9ab5-4bef-ab1e-052a3709d16e",
                                "sense_id": "093d1698-033c-3e27-9752-623bb4855f67",
                                "text": "And finally I thank my kin, who have seen past fortune and misfortune with the inconcussible evenness of love."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "927814db-ee1c-421c-aa5d-fb786c4ba8fc",
                                "sense_id": "093d1698-033c-3e27-9752-623bb4855f67",
                                "text": "One grants properties [Eigenschaften] in the inconcussible certitude of an accord"
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "bffa6017-54b2-3e35-a3f2-cf9a07a06ebb",
                        "entry_id": "bcf52278-0c3a-325f-9a25-c260155c982c",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Unshakable;",
                            "Unassailable; incontrovertible."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "49fe7a26-221d-4458-83c7-5fbf00b4c320",
                                "sense_id": "bffa6017-54b2-3e35-a3f2-cf9a07a06ebb",
                                "text": "an inconcussible fact"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "48eb3099-9f47-4558-8e11-4d27e5ab78f5",
                                "sense_id": "bffa6017-54b2-3e35-a3f2-cf9a07a06ebb",
                                "text": "The judgment has gone forth as valid and inconcussible, in spite of assessors impugning it, who belong to the highest order of religious teachers recognized by the State."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "b6543ef6-bcc9-4c55-944c-25cf6117b67c",
                                "sense_id": "bffa6017-54b2-3e35-a3f2-cf9a07a06ebb",
                                "text": "The weak point in the theory of genetic evolution is not that it transgresses any inconcussible principle of sound philosophy, but that it cannot be satisfactorily squared with the facts of nature."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "893d2855-9081-4aee-98fe-379b32938c61",
                                "sense_id": "bffa6017-54b2-3e35-a3f2-cf9a07a06ebb",
                                "text": "In the face of \"words so plainly put together,\" the fact that slavery was neither sin nor abomination was \"inconcussible'.\""
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
